    "question": {
      ":question/id": "2c7b9726-0b90-580c-b0b7-d966c549e769",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following matrices are lower triangular matrices?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The matrices $A$, $B$ and $C$ are lower triangular matrices since all the entries above the main diagonal are zeros.\n\nThe matrices $D$ and $E$ are *not* lower triangular matrices since they each have a non-zero element above the main diagonal: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}_{34} & =-5\\ne 0 \\\\ {e}_{34} & =7\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
