      ":question/id": "a0d83bd6-6559-547b-9784-6284bce4bcfa",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following matrices are lower triangular matrices?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The matrices $A$ and $B$ are lower triangular matrices since all the entries above the main diagonal are zeros.\n\nThe matrices $C$ and $D$ and $E$ are *not* lower triangular matrices since they each have a non-zero element above the main diagonal: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{12} & =-1\\ne 0 \\\\ {d}_{23} & =-1\\ne 0 \\\\ {e}_{23} & =-9\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
